{"title":"2014 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f4c825d5dd7e3c9485ef03ca1d225a2838ed974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0&lt;a_1&lt;a_2&lt;\\cdots \\quad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"12\" /> be an infinite sequence of positive integers, Prove that there exists a unique integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340797a8fa9f1a06b10ce9e764998830b15ca755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> such that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/4/0c463e53d0ab2ad520551056d74fad908d859cb5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_n&lt;\\frac{a_0+a_1+\\cdots + a_n}{n}\\le a_{n+1}.\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53f12ec5ee4a2e5304810da76fbb60e0d3cf46c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> be an integer. Consider an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f761f7fc79f2bec21a2f31c896840d6f36cdc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\times n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> chessboard consisting of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> unit squares. A configuration of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> rooks on this board is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/652d535aa6850153c57be651aa9fc00c29a6f4c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$peaceful$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" /> if every row and every column contains exactly one rook. Find the greatest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that, for each peaceful configuration of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> rooks, there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/e/97e11746bde904a399f341e9c7ee8f328c526c8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\times k$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> square which does not contain a rook on any of its <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5c83cc0c639fc2ed843bbe2d3d209fb478b104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> squares.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Convex quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/3/053c047438548d9beffe9daac64f0224990eb2d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ABC}=\\angle{CDA}=90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"184\" height=\"13\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the foot of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> lie on sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/3486553bff11d01f6bed5112632a383888fad819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{SCT}$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f7fdb3d9a89e2d7864c895d94972778862131a4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle{CHS}-\\angle{CSB}=90^{\\circ},\\quad \\angle{THC}-\\angle{DTC} = 90^{\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"395\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Prove that line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/6/016bdc0a88d05ab229f3a0701478134682a453da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{TSH}.$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> lie on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> of acute-angled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/3779979c286710a8a4fbb3454dd1265694818fff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{PAB}=\\angle{BCA}$\" width=\"135\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/e/83eb18bf78cccbc8d066299cd6df96ea5901b4bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CAQ}=\\angle{ABC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lie on lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/7563031eab26ad18658cf2f6a8e4948861bb9013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, respectively, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aafc7e3cc1eafce5e16d3a45250eeda7b1a6526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" />. Prove that lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/8068607716f3c2549af1dc978d77a422ca7201dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/3/ba369b33271c6fb52789f86292cc68559a2e0411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CN$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> intersect on the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the Bank of Cape Town issues coins of denomination <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c13e6f961c9bff23cc9fe69c37050986eb4b38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"10\" height=\"21\" />. Given a finite collection of such coins (of not necessarily different denominations) with total value at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/e/a4e2fc9b786cbb2704693973a4c88a923ccc13be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99+\\tfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"53\" height=\"23\" />, prove that it is possible to split this collection into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> or fewer groups, such that each group has total value at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A set of lines in the plane is in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/0/b80a87958772b79b99361a043408f25b4588fa71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{general position}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" /> if no two are parallel and no three pass through the same point. A set of lines in general position cuts the plane into regions, some of which have finite are; we call these its <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/2/ac2f2e56f28020a4813cacc3439cc9502c902924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{finite regions}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" />. Prove that for all sufficiently large <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, in any set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> lines in general position it is possible to colour at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b58afccd87d49e39a6e850d3121001b0266ae52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> of the lines blue in such a way that none of its finite regions has a completely blue boundary.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO\" title=\"2014 IMO\">2014 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2013 IMO Problems\">2013 IMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2015 IMO Problems\">2015 IMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017064244\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 298/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 854/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 74/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9166/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    9.239      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    9.239      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13394:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017064244 and revision id 149509. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}